      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's much better. The depth is getting there. \n\nOne thing though—when the editors look at these reviews, they really look for a certain level of structural formality. They expect a very systematic breakdown where every single aspect of the study is categorized under its own specific heading. It helps them navigate the critique quickly.\n\nCould you do one more pass to make the review even more comprehensive? I'd like you to break the critique down into many distinct, granular sections—covering everything from the material preparation and the spectroscopic setup to the specific statistical models used and the final discussion. \n\nI really need this to look like a highly detailed, multi-sectioned formal review. Just please don't do the \"empty heading\" thing I mentioned before; I need every section to actually contain substantive, critical points. I just want it to be very organized and segmented into many parts so it doesn't look like one big wall of text.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
